## Opt-in remote (MP Testing)

Use only when the user explicitly chose remote MP Testing + Live MP APIs in **`.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/test/y-tst-e2e-pmroo.mdc`** pre-flight.

### Configuration (`.env.e2e.local`)

- Path: **`.env.e2e.local`** (repo root)
- Load: `set -a && source .env.e2e.local && set +a` from the project root (or Python `dotenv` in scripts)
- **Do not** paste secrets into chat or reports
- **Do not** edit **`.env.e2e.local`** unless the user explicitly asks

| Variable | Use |
|----------|-----|
| `MARKETPLACE_URL` | PM UI base (testing MP) |
| `MARKETPLACE_JWT` | Bearer for **remote** chat API + MP API (`Authorization: Bearer <jwt>`) |
| `MARKETPLACE_TEST_EMAIL` / `PASSWORD` | PM UI login |
| `CLIENT`, `CLIENT_ID`, `LOCATION` | Defaults for WO / client context |
| `N8N_API_KEY` | Optional read-only n8n inspection (never log) |

Legacy fallbacks: `VENDOROO_ADMIN_AUTH_BEARER` in repo **`.env`** — prefer **per-client** tokens when testing client-specific behavior ([`docs/tickets/VAP-2159/testing-clients.md`](../../../docs/tickets/VAP-2159/testing-clients.md)).

### Standard payload (remote, non-streaming)

```json
{
  "user_id": "<pm-user-uuid or stable test id>",
  "session_id": "<NEW uuid per trial>",
  "user_type": "property_manager",
  "source": "Web App",
  "client_id": 935,
  "context_info": "",
  "stream": false,
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "for #WO-00139 tenant is home tomorrow 2–4pm. Please have vendor call tenant.",
      "meta_data": {
        "attachments": []
      }
    }
  ],
  "meta_data": {
    "auth_bearer": "Bearer <jwt>",
    "client_id": 935,
    "work_order_number": "WO-00139",
    "job_token": "<uuid from request-id=>",
    "location_id": null,
    "session_id": "<same uuid as top-level session_id>",
    "source": "Web App"
  }
}
```

### curl template (remote)

```bash
SESSION="$(uuidgen)"
curl -sS "https://api-testing-marketplace.vendoroo.ai/chat/api/chat" \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer ${MARKETPLACE_JWT}" \
  -d "{ ... }"
```

### Sanity checks (remote)

- WO exists: `GET {apiBase}/api/WorkOrder/{jobToken}` or `ById/{workOrderId}` with **`MARKETPLACE_JWT`**
- **`client_id`** on WO matches payload `meta_data.client_id`

